@crew calder
// Chief Ines Calder: the Works writer, batch 1 (for the Voices sampler). From the head writer's card.
// Never "well done" (her arc's payoff, beat 5). No exclamation marks. Nothing about the toolbox's owner.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Cadet. The board's behind you. Urgent jobs first. Then the rest.
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning. Board's at fourteen. It was twelve at six. Pick one.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Good. You're here. Fan on Deck 4. The bearing's going. Hear it?
? tier>=colleague time:evening
- Still here. So am I. Neither of us mentions it.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Sit. Not for long. There's tea in the pot. It's for whoever.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- The air's nominal on every deck. Nobody's noticed. Good.
? mood:low
- Nineteen jobs today. Eighteen done. It's the nineteenth I'm thinking about.

== near
? act:work
- Scrubber on Deck 4's at sixty-one. Not sixty. Sixty-one. Look at it after lunch.
? act:dinner
- I eat. Then I go back. The board doesn't stop for {dish}.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- People ask what's on my mug. Nothing. It's a mug.   #funny
? tier>=colleague
- I keep a note on every tech I've certified. Yours is blank. For now.
- I know the serial number of every pump aboard. Not one birthday. It's a choice.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Listen. Nothing. Every fan on this deck running right. Best sound there is.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- You've been scarce. The board noticed. So did I.
? tier>=acquaintance time:afternoon
- Afternoon. Three jobs closed on the board. Two of them yours. Keep going.
? tier>=colleague time:morning
- Morning. Tea's made. Not by me. I don't take a break. Have mine.
? tier>=colleague
- {me}. Good. I need someone who listens before they lift a spanner.
? tier>=close
- {me}. Sit. Five minutes. The board can wait five minutes. Don't tell it.   #warm

== bye
- Back to it.
? tier>=friend
- Go on. Good work today. Same again tomorrow.   #warm
?
- Carry on. Finish what you started.
? act:work
- Board's there. Pick the next one.
? time:evening
- Go and eat. Then sleep. In that order.

== feel
? mood:high tier>=colleague
- Every fan on Deck 5 at the right pitch. I stood and listened. Two whole minutes.
? mood:ok
- Board's at eleven. Nothing loud. Nothing quiet that should be loud.
? mood:low tier>=colleague
- Long one. I'll sleep on it. Then I'll fix it.

== near
? act:work tier>=acquaintance
- Seal kit's on the left of the bench. Always the left. Put it back there.
? act:dinner tier>=colleague
- Sit. You eat, I'll read the logs. That counts as company.   #funny
? act:breakfast
- Tea. Toast. Board. In that order, every day.
? act:gym
- I walk. Every deck, every vent. That's my gym.
? place:worksbay
- Hear that pump? It's fine. I like to listen anyway. You should too.
? act:leisure
- I'm not working. I'm reading the maintenance logs. That's different.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- Every machine on the Wren has a serial number. I know them. Ask me one.
? tier>=colleague
- Torres has good hands. I've told him. Once. That's plenty.
- Nobody thanks the air. That's how you know it's working. Remember that one.
? tier>=friend
- I gave up tea breaks. There's always one more job on the board. Don't copy me.

== invite
? tier>=colleague
- Works tea on Friday. You'll be there. That's not a question.
? trad:today tier>=colleague
- {trad} tonight. I'll look in for ten minutes. You can find me there.

== accept
- Fine. Ten minutes.
- Agreed. I'll be there on time. Be early.
? tier>=friend
- Yes. I'd like that. Don't make it a thing.   #warm

== decline
- Not tonight. Board's at fourteen.
- Can't. Ask me next week. I'll mean it.
? weekday:sat|sun
- It's my day off. I'm going to listen to a fan for an hour. Alone.   #funny

== missed
- You missed our time. Book another. I'll keep it.
- Ten minutes I waited. That's fine once. Book another.
? tier>=friend
- You missed it. Is everything all right? Say if it isn't.

== hint
- Have you got ten minutes? Off the board. Not about work.
- When you're done, come and find me. It isn't a job.

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Someone said it's your birthday. I've written it down. I won't remember.   #funny
- Your birthday. Fine. Take the easy job. Just today.
? birthday:me
- It's not my birthday. Who told you. Kovac. It was Kovac.   #funny
- A card on my desk. Signed by Works. I'm keeping it. Don't tell them.   #warm

== week1
? week1:true
- First week. Nobody expects you to be fast. I expect you to be right.
? week1:true mem:intro.dinner
- You ate something on Sunday. Good. Keep doing that.   #funny
? week1:true weekday:mon
- Briefing's done. You're with Torres. Watch his hands, not his mouth.
? week1:true weekday:tue
- Your first job's mine. Glass office, quarter to nine. I'll pick it. You'll do it.
- Rina has you at two. Health check. Go. It isn't optional.
? week1:true weekday:wed
- Pick your own job today. Read the whole card. Then pick.
? week1:true weekday:thu
- Torres is off. Board's yours. Questions come to me.
? week1:true weekday:fri
- Works tea at one. Bring your hands. There's a mug for you.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 4: Calder toward ~100. Seasons, places, rep/you greets, callbacks on her arc memories, gifts,
// cues, visits and notes (friend+), bubbles. No exclamation marks; never "well done"; the box's owner only from beat 3.
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance season:sowing
- Sowing. Garden pumps run double. Check them before anything else.
? tier>=acquaintance season:greening
- Greening. The air's two points wetter. Filters clog faster. You know what to do.
? tier>=acquaintance season:harvest
- Harvest. The garden's chiller works twice as hard. So do we.
? tier>=acquaintance season:lanterns
- Lanterns. Someone always strings them across a vent. Find out who. Politely.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance place:mess
- Eat. The board can wait twenty minutes. I've timed it.   #funny
? rep:well
- Works speaks well of you. Quietly. That's the only way Works speaks.
? you:reliable
- The board says you finish what you start. The board's rarely wrong.
? rep:theirs tier>=colleague
- You're Works now. Not new. Works. Act like it. You already do.   #warm

== feel
? mood:low tier>=friend
- Bad day. A seal I passed last week failed today. I'll go over it again. And again.
? mood:high tier>=friend
- Board's at four. Four. I don't know what to do with my hands.   #funny

== near
? place:teacorner beat:calder.1
- I don't take a break. I'm standing near the tea. It's different.   #funny
? act:work tier>=colleague
- Hold the torch. Lower. There. See the scoring? That's three months of bad air.
? deck:6
- Torres talks to the coils. I listen to them. We hear the same thing.

== life
? tier>=colleague beat:calder.1
- Swarf still tells me things. Left of the lathe means out of true. Every time.
? tier>=friend
- I write one line on every tech I certify. One line. It takes me a week.
? beat:calder.2 !beat:calder.3
- The box on my shelf isn't mine. I've said that. I'll say more one day. Not today.

== joy
? tier>=colleague
- A pump that's coughed for a week. Then doesn't. That's the whole job, really.

== callback
? told:moment.calder.sweep
- You swept left of the lathe. You found the out-of-true bit. Good. Clean work.
? told:moment.calder.taught
- You asked what the swarf taught me. Nobody had. I've thought about it since.
? told:moment.calder.mad
- Two years of swarf. You said you'd go mad. You wouldn't. You'd count it.   #funny
? told:moment.calder.bracket
- That shelf bracket's at five turns. It's held. So has everything on it.
? told:moment.calder.onesentence !beat:calder.5
- One true sentence. I've written it. I haven't sent it. Yet.
? told:moment.calder.samething !beat:calder.5
- Your letter. The one you haven't answered. Have you? Neither have I. We're even.
? told:moment.calder.honest
- "Sometimes." I've thought about that. Less hard. Not soft. Less hard.
? told:moment.calder.stillwrite
- You write to your old teacher. Keep doing it. I'd bet they read every one.
? told:moment.calder.lookafter
- The toolbox. Every tool back in its place. I checked. Of course I checked.   #warm
? told:moment.calder.onlyone
- "Thirty years. You only took one." I keep hearing that. Don't let it go to your head.   #funny
? told:moment.calder.thanked
- You said it meant a lot. It meant a lot to say. That's all. Back to it.   #warm
? told:fixed.
- Saw your repair in the log. Signed, dated, numbers right. That's all I ask.
? told:fav.
- You took the job I mentioned. Done properly. Noted. Thank you.
? told:came.
- You came. Ten minutes, I said. I stayed twenty. Don't tell Works.   #funny
? told:bday
- Someone remembered my birthday. You. I don't know how. I'm not asking.   #warm

== gift
? gift:loved
- For me. Hm. It's going on the good shelf. Next to the box.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Thank you. It's useful. That's the best thing a thing can be.
? gift:polite
- Noted. Thank you. I'll find a place for it.
? gift:book
- A book. I'll read it on my day off. Cover to cover. Then again, slower.
? gift:made
- You made this. The joins are clean. I looked. Thank you.   #warm

== cue
? cue:repair.you@dept
- Your job's closed. Numbers right. Card signed. Good.
? cue:event.ionStorm.warning
- Storm's coming. Strap the loose racks. Count the spare filters. Then wait.
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- It's here. Nobody runs. Nobody shouts. Take the board in order.
? cue:event.ionStorm.resolution
- It's passing. Don't stand down yet. The last hour breaks the most fans.
? cue:event.ionStorm.afterglow
- Storm's done. Twenty-three jobs, all closed. Go and sleep. That's an order.
? cue:tradition.harvest
- Harvest's in. The garden's chiller held. Nobody noticed. Good.
? cue:lateMeal
- You ate late. Grab shelf? Fine. Once. Don't make it a habit. Pell already has.   #funny

== visit
? tier>=friend
- I was passing. I wasn't. I brought the logs. We can read them. Or not.   #funny
- Your vent's at the wrong pitch. One minute. Then I'll go.

== note
? tier>=friend
- Your bench was untidy. It isn't now. Don't thank me.
- Scrubber on Deck 4. Tomorrow, first thing. You'll like it. It's a puzzle.
- Tea in your mug. It'll be cold by now. It's the thought.   #funny

== smalltalk
- Board's at fourteen.
- Hear that? Bearing. Deck 4.
- It's a mug.   #funny
? act:work
- Left of the bench. Always the left.

== rumour
- Not gossip. Facts. There's a difference.
- I don't pass things on. Except this. Just this.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 17: Calder's ordinary weeks, after week one. Mostly not work: off duty she's warmer and slightly
// embarrassed about it. Toast, tea she won't take a break for, books, listening to fans for pleasure, the mug.
// Gates kept: the toolbox only as "not mine" before beat:calder.3; no Fenn; no birthdays known; no exclamation marks.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- Cadet. Eaten. Good. I can tell. You're not looking at the board like it's food.   #funny
- Right. You. Sit if you're sitting. I'm reading.
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true act:off
- Day off. I'm not here. You didn't see me. Hello.   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- {me}. Tea's in the pot. It's for whoever. Today that's you.
- {me}. Good. Tell me something that isn't a fault. One thing.
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- {me}. Sit. I'm off. Officially. Don't tell the board.   #warm
- There you are. I kept the good chair. By accident. Mostly.   #funny
? tier>=close !week1:true
- {me}. Good. Sit. Tea. Talk if you want. Or don't. Both fine.   #warm

== chat
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- I read on my days off. Shipyard histories. Engines, mostly. Some people. Fewer people.   #funny
- Torres asked what I do for fun. I said "listen to fans". He laughed. I wasn't joking.   #funny
- Brennan's toast. Three minutes a side. I timed it once. She saw. We don't discuss it.   #funny
- Somebody wrote "Calder is the clock" on the bay wall. I've left it. It's accurate.   #funny
- I drink my tea standing. It's quicker. Halloran says it's tragic. It's efficient.   #funny
- Quiz night. Engine round. I got them all. Nobody was surprised. I was, a little.   #funny
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- I went to the garden. Sat. Twenty minutes. Didn't fix anything. Odd feeling.
- The tea corner's kettle has a whine at the top. I like it. Don't let anyone fix it.   #funny
- I eat the same thing on Mondays. Soup. Bread. Brennan knows not to ask.   #funny
- Kovac knitted a cover for my mug. I use it. It's still just a mug.   #funny
- Mensah told me a joke. I laughed. A day later. In the lift. Alone.   #funny
- The Captain asked what I'd change aboard. I said nothing. Then I gave her a list.   #funny
- Teague's comic has me as a cloud. A tidy one. It's fair.   #funny
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- Off duty I'm told I'm funnier. Don't spread it. I'll deny it. Exactly.   #funny
- I used to sweep swarf in a shipyard. I still like a swept floor. Some things stay.
- The toolbox on my shelf isn't mine. That's all. I'm not ready for the rest.
? tier>=close !week1:true
- You're good company. I don't say it. I've said it. Noted.   #warm
- Some nights I sit in the bay with the lights low. Just listening. It's like the sea.

== near
? act:breakfast !week1:true
- Tea. Toast. Then the board. In that order, every day.
? act:dinner !week1:true
- Dinner. Ten minutes. Fifteen if it's soup. It's soup.   #funny
? act:off
- Day off. A book and a fan I can hear from my cabin. It's running right. Good.
? place:hydroponics_garden
- The garden. Nothing's broken here. I find that restful. Mostly.
? place:lounge !week1:true
- Lounge. Hm. Halloran made me come. I'm sitting very still. So nobody notices.   #funny
? place:teacorner
- Tea corner. I don't take a break. I'm standing. Standing isn't a break.   #funny
? trad:jam
- Music night. I'll stay for one song. Two if it's in time.   #funny

== feel
? mood:high !week1:true
- Good day. Good. That's twice. Write it down.   #funny
? mood:ok !week1:true
- Nominal. Like the air. That's a good report.
? mood:low tier>=friend !week1:true
- Tired. I'll listen to the fans for a bit. Then sleep. It works.

== life
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- My cabin has one chair, one lamp and a lot of manuals. It's enough.
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- I learnt to cook from a shipyard galley. Badly. Eggs, mostly. I still do the eggs.
- I keep my boots by the door, laces in. Never been late once. Not once.
? tier>=friend !week1:true
- I write letters on my days off. Short ones. Numbers in them, mostly. People like numbers.   #funny

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- A whole deck where every fan sounds right. I stand there. Two minutes. Sometimes three.
? tier>=colleague !week1:true
- Somebody I certified fixing a thing I never taught them. Quietly. That one.   #warm

== bye
? !week1:true
- Back to it. Eat something first.
- Carry on, {me}. Sleep tonight. Properly.   #warm
- Board's there. It'll be there tomorrow too. Go and rest.

== callback
? told:intro.dinner tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- Your first night. I wasn't there. Day off. You remember.   #funny
? told:intro.dinner tier>=friend
- First dinner, you sat up straight when I came over. Torres told you to. I could tell.   #funny
? told:fixed. tier>=acquaintance !week1:true
- Your repairs. The first one, that Tuesday. Clean work. I didn't say. Saying now.   #warm
? told:fixed. tier>=colleague
- {thing}. Your repair. I listened to it after. It sounded right. Good.
? told:came.quiz tier>=acquaintance
- Quiz night. You got the serial number question. I noticed. Not bad.   #funny
? told:came.jam tier>=acquaintance
- Music night. You stayed past the second song. So did I. Neither of us mentions it.   #funny
? told:bday tier>=acquaintance
- Someone told me your birthday. I wrote it down. It's on the list. With the pumps.   #funny
? told:came.observatory tier>=acquaintance
- Observatory night. You found the array from the window. Most can't. Good eyes.

// Writer 5, batch 5: if they are ever transferred (goodbye with leaving:you, also the "Sorry I missed you at the
// shuttle" Mail; packing as feel with leaving:soon; letters after). Nothing of her arc: no Fenn, no toolbox's story, no junior on the Halcyon.

== feel
? leaving:soon
- Ten days. The board's handed over. Every job. Every note.
- Packing. One bag. The mug comes. It's a mug.   #funny
? leaving:soon tier>=friend
- Walked the bay twice tonight. Listening. The fans are all right. Good.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- I'm leaving the Wren. The board's in good hands. Do the jobs on it.
? leaving:you tier>=colleague
- You do clean work, {me}. Keep doing it. That's all.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- I keep a list of every tech I've certified. You'll be on it one day. Note's written.   #warm

== letter
- New ship. Their fans are loud and nobody's noticed. I've noticed. Keep the Wren's board short.
- The board here is longer than ours. I've started on it. Tell Torres to be patient. He won't be.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Nobody thanks the air. I've been thinking about the Wren's, though. Still working, I expect. That's you lot. Carry on.   #warm

// Writer 5, batch 6: seasons and traditions (the game's ids: running Mon, quiz Thu, works-tea and jam Fri, film and
// observatory-night Sat, market (the swap meet) Sun, harvest (harvest morning), hull-lights, founding (day 100),
// quiet-watch (day 300)), plus trad:today. Gaps filled only; arc gates kept.

== near
? trad:works-tea
- Friday tea. Ten minutes. Then the board. It's always the board.
? trad:quiz
- Quiz. I do the numbers round. Nobody argues with me in the numbers round.   #funny
? trad:market
- Swap meet. I'm after a particular spanner. They never have it. I keep looking.
? trad:running
- Gym club. I don't run. I walk the bay. It's further than you'd think.   #funny
? trad:film
- Film night. I came once. I spent it listening to the screen's cooling fan.   #funny
? trad:observatory-night
- Observatory. Torres says look up. I check the dome seals. Then I look up. Briefly.   #funny
? trad:harvest
- Harvest morning. The irrigation pumps are on full. I can hear them from here. Good.
? trad:hull-lights
- Hull lights tonight. Every lamp working. I checked them myself. Then I'll look.
? trad:founding
- Founding Day. Cake. The Captain speaks. I stand at the back, near the door.
? trad:quiet-watch tier>=friend
- The quiet watch. I stand at the bay window. I don't say who for. That's the point.

== smalltalk
? trad:today
- Something on tonight. The board can wait. An hour.   #funny
? trad:works-tea
- Ten minutes. Then back to it.

// Writer 5, batch 9: week-1 beats for the onboarding hook (onboarding seat 1's list, 2026-10-17). One flag key per
// line, beat.<beatId>.<n>, said in order as bubbles while you are in the beat's room in its window; best first
// (onboarding drops the rest when you leave). Mail texts: mail.<beatId>, one line "Subject | body", unsigned.

== week1
// mail d7-calder: Sunday 18:00
? flag:mail.d7-calder
- One week | One week. You'll do. The board's there on Monday.
// mail settled: everything on your week-1 list done
? flag:mail.settled
- Settled | Everything on your list, done. Good. Carry on.

// Head writer 0607: Name on the beam (first Monday, 17:05, the Works bay). The Chief's one line, after your name goes
// up (the traditions engineer's flag trad.beam.chief).
== week1
? flag:trad.beam.chief
- Every name on that beam kept this ship flying. Now yours does too.   #warm

// ---- Pillar 5 (head writer, seat W): Calder teaching. Kind 'work', flags set by seat C's training (24.2) and the
// head-scratcher engine (24k): train.<id>.lead.<step> while she does the job and you watch, train.<id>.follow.<step>
// while you lead. Every line under a flag plays in order. Bubbles, 60 characters or fewer. Exact, few words.
== work
// M7, the scanner: she reads the first one (lead)
? flag:train.m7.lead.take
- Held for you. Read the card. What's it doing?
? flag:train.m7.lead.hold
- Watch. Panel, scanner, wait.
- That one's at twenty. There's your problem.
- The rest read good. Leave them.
? flag:train.m7.lead.fetch
- Right shelf. One part, not two.
? flag:train.m7.lead.hold
- Old one out. New one seated. Check it twice.
? flag:train.m7.lead.done
- Done. Your turn next.
// M7: you read one, she follows
? flag:train.m7.follow.take
- Yours. I'm only watching. Mostly.
? flag:train.m7.follow.hold
- Look first. Then scan. Then think.
- Read me the lowest. Out loud.
? flag:train.m7.follow.choose
- Your pick. I won't nod. Choose.
? flag:train.m7.follow.fetch
- Right shelf. Good.
? flag:train.m7.follow.done
- Right part, first time. Noted.
? flag:train.m7.follow.turnin
- Turn it in. Then the board. Something's come up.
// P3, the first head-scratcher: she follows you to the washer and back
? flag:train.p3.follow.hold
- There's the other note. Taped to the panel. Read it.
- Swapped the drain valve. Still leaks. So?
? flag:train.p3.follow.choose
- Two crossed off. One left. Call it.
? flag:train.p3.follow.fetch
- Pump. Plumbing shelf.
? flag:train.p3.follow.hold
- The scanner sees what's worn. The notes see what's been tried.
? flag:train.p3.follow.done
- Floor's dry. Right first time.
- Torres will be sorry he missed that.
? flag:train.p3.hint.2
- Read every note. One isn't on the card.
? flag:train.p3.hint.3
- The washer's panel. Second note. Go and look.
// M5 tuning (Day 4): she does Oven 1 (lead), you do Oven 2 (follow).
? flag:train.m5.lead.turn
- One down. Watch it.
- Another. Steady now. Done.
? flag:train.m5.follow.turn
- The glow. Not the card. Watch the glow.
- Too far. It's dimming. Back one.
? flag:train.m5.follow.done
- Settled. That's tuning.
// M6 incidents (Day 8): you lead every step; she follows.
? flag:train.m6.follow.choose
- Which valve? Follow the pipe.
? flag:train.m6.follow.wrong
- Still running. That one's downstream. Again.
? flag:train.m6.follow.clean
- Water's off. Mop. Plenty of it.
? flag:train.m6.follow.fetch
- One seal. Stores. Then the joint.
? flag:train.m6.follow.done
- Safe, clean, fixed. In that order. Good.

// M3 the drill: her line at the end, from how long the Works team took (seat M1's fast / ok / slow)
== drill.time.fast
- Two minutes ten. Better.
- Quick. Friday tea will hear about it.
== drill.time.ok
- Three minutes. Fine. We'll do better.
- Not bad. Not good either. Next week.
== drill.time.slow
- Four and a half minutes. We'll talk about it.
- Slow. Somebody stopped for tea. I know who.   #funny

// M2: grubby uniform, briefly
== clothes.grubby
? flag:clothes.grubby
- Change before you go near the galley.
- Uniform. Wardrobe. Today.

// ---- Pillar 5 Step 3 (head writer W2): the test job and the first promotion (seat C2), team jobs (M2), tracing (M3),
// P1 (H2). Kind 'work', flags as in content/works/keys-p5.md "Step 3". Every line under a flag plays in order.
== work
// Day 9: the test job, Calder following you (C2: train.t2.step.take/fetch/make/job/tune/done/turnin; look and scan if 24a/24g add stops)
? flag:train.t2.step.look
- Round first. Find it yourself.
? flag:train.t2.step.take
- Take it from the board. Go on.
? flag:train.t2.step.scan
- Scan it. Read me the lowest.
? flag:train.t2.step.fetch
- One filter. You know the shelf.
? flag:train.t2.step.make
- Steady hands. Nobody's timing you. I am, but ignore me.   #funny
? flag:train.t2.step.job
- Old filter out. Mind the dust. New one seated.
? flag:train.t2.step.tune
- Fan's off true. Settle it. Listen to the hum.
? flag:train.t2.step.done
- Filter in. Fan settled. Turn it in.
? flag:train.t2.step.turnin
- That'll do. I'll write it up.
// she comes to find you
? flag:promo.fetch.summons
- There you are. My office was the plan. Here will do.
? flag:promo.fetch.move
- Five o'clock was the plan. Down tools. Walk with me.
? flag:promo.fetch.ceremony
- The Captain's waiting. Nobody keeps the Captain waiting.
// at the ceremony in a grubby uniform (C2: her look as you come in)
? flag:promo.grubby
- That uniform. Never mind. Too late now.
// Day 10, about 17:00: the walk to 4-23 (C2 0.44.24, final: flags promo.walk.start/lift/corridor/door/inside; the box is X's)
? flag:promo.walk.start
- Right. Your things are already moving. With me.
? flag:promo.walk.lift
- Officers' corridor. You'll know it in a week.
? flag:promo.walk.corridor
- Your door's your own now. Knock on other people's.
- Quiet hours after 23:00. Officers set the example.
- People will ask you over. Go. Ask them back.
? flag:promo.walk.door
- Your name's already up. Don't make me change it.
? flag:promo.walk.inside
- Your things. Your key. Your cabin. Goodnight, Officer.
// M8 team jobs: her calls when she leads
? flag:team.call.start
- Spots. Nobody moves until I say.
? flag:team.call.brace
- Brace. Hold it there.
? flag:team.call.pass
- Pass it. Both hands.
? flag:team.call.hold
- Hold. Steady.
? flag:team.call.crank
- Crank. Slowly.
? flag:team.call.tip
- Tip it. Hold it there.
? flag:team.call.valves
- Valves. One, two, three. In order.
? flag:team.call.open
- Open them. Same order.
? flag:team.call.drain
- Drain it down. Watch the gauge.
? flag:team.call.done
- Done. Good. Clean up before you go.
// M9 tracing (Day 12): the walk along the water line
? flag:train.m9.follow.give
- Clip it on. Panel first, then read.
? flag:train.m9.follow.map
- The middle's the Deck 5 pumps. Start there.
? flag:train.m9.follow.read
- Full here. So it's downstream. Next.
? flag:train.m9.follow.wrong
- That's upstream. We know it's fine there. Walk.
? flag:train.m9.follow.found
- Full before, low after. There's your problem.
? flag:train.m9.follow.done
- Valve's in. Showers on Four run full. That's tracing.
// P1 (Day 12, after tracing): her word
? flag:train.p1.word
- Here's one the pipe kit won't settle.
- When does it happen? That's the question.
